cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use MAGNUS in your work, please cite it with the metadata below.
  A paper describing the code is in preparation; this file will be updated
  with that reference as soon as it exists.
title: "MAGNUS: forward model and Bayesian inference for the thermal X-ray emission of magnetized neutron stars"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "de Lima"
    given-names: "Rafael C. R."
    affiliation: "Universidade do Estado de Santa Catarina (UDESC); ICRANet, Università degli Studi di Ferrara"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-18
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22760147
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22760147
    description: "Concept DOI of the Zenodo archive; resolves to the latest version"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22844147
    description: "DOI of version 0.2.0"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22760148
    description: "DOI of version 0.1.0"
abstract: >-
  MAGNUS is a forward model and Bayesian inference code for the thermal X-ray
  emission of strongly magnetized neutron stars. A two-mode magnetized hydrogen
  atmosphere solver, with exact normal modes including vacuum polarization,
  produces angle-resolved specific-intensity tables I(E, mu, theta_B); a C++
  relativistic ray-tracing engine with exact Schwarzschild light bending, a
  two-pole surface temperature law and dipolar surface fields turns them into
  phase-resolved spectra and pulse profiles; and an affine-invariant ensemble
  MCMC fits them to phase-energy event data. Source code:
  https://github.com/RafaelCRdeLima/MAGNUS
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/RafaelCRdeLima/MAGNUS"
keywords:
  - neutron stars
  - magnetized atmospheres
  - radiative transfer
  - general relativity
  - X-ray astronomy
  - Bayesian inference

